[size=4][u]All Ships with Filters[/u][/size]

Adds an [b]All Ships with Filters[/b] tab to the [b]Property Owned[/b] menu in the map. The tab shows all owned ships in three sections: [b]Fleets[/b], [b]Stations with Assigned Ships[/b] (subordinate ships only, without module or construction rows), and [b]Unassigned Ships[/b]. Supports multi-dimensional filtering by ship type, size, sector, dock status, default behaviour, current order, and failed orders.

[size=3][u][b]Features[/b][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] [b]All Ships tab[/b]: A dedicated tab in the Property Owned menu lists every owned ship in three sections - Fleets, Stations with Assigned Ships, and Unassigned Ships - using the same ship rows as the vanilla view (hull bars, action buttons, sub-expansion).
[*] [b]Stations section[/b]: Shows only the subordinate ships assigned to each station, hiding module and construction rows for a cleaner list.
[*] [b]Multi-dimensional filtering[/b]: Add up to one filter per available dimension. Each filter row has a category dropdown and, once a category is selected, a value dropdown. Multiple filter slots appear automatically; remove a slot by setting its category back to None.
[*] [b]Filter dimensions[/b]: [b]Type[/b] (ship purpose), [b]Size[/b] (hull class), [b]Sector[/b], [b]Docked[/b] (yes/no), [b]Default Behaviour[/b], [b]Current Order[/b], [b]Failed Orders[/b].
[*] [b]Fleet handling[/b]: A fleet is shown whenever the fleet commander or at least one subordinate passes the active filters. Fleet unit group entries are always preserved so the expand/collapse button remains functional.
[*] [b]Expand/collapse all[/b]: When the list contains expandable entries (fleets or stations with subordinates), a master +/- button appears in the filter header row to expand or collapse all at once.
[*] [b]Compatible with X4 8.00 and 9.00[/b].
[/list]
