[size=3][u][b]Usage[/b][/u][/size]

Open the map, switch to the [b]Property Owned[/b] panel, and click the [b]All Ships with Filters[/b] tab in the tab strip.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-AllShipsWithFilters/refs/heads/main/docs/images/all_ships.png[/img]

[size=3][u][i]Filter rows[/i][/u][/size]

The top of the tab contains one or more [b]filter rows[/b]. Each row has:
[list]
[*] A [b]category dropdown[/b] - choose the dimension to filter by (Type, Size, Sector, Docked, Default Behaviour, Current Order, Failed Orders). Setting this back to None removes only that slot; the remaining slots are preserved. Changing it to a different category removes all slots after it, since their value selections may no longer be meaningful.
[*] A [b]value dropdown[/b] - appears once a category is chosen; select the specific value to match. Choosing None here shows all ships regardless of that dimension's value.
[/list]
Additional filter slots appear automatically when all existing slots have an active category. All active filters are applied simultaneously (AND logic).

[size=3][u][i]Expand/collapse all[/i][/u][/size]

When the ship list contains expandable entries (fleet leaders or stations with subordinates), a [b]+/-[/b] button appears in the filter header row. Clicking it expands or collapses every expandable entry at once.

[size=3][u][i]Sections[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] [b]Fleets[/b]: Fleet leaders and their subordinates. A fleet is visible if the commander or any subordinate passes the filter.
[*] [b]Stations with Assigned Ships[/b]: Stations that have at least one assigned ship passing the filter, showing only the subordinate ships.
[*] [b]Unassigned Ships[/b]: Ships not assigned to a fleet or station, filtered by the active filter.
[/list]
[size=3][u][i]Extension options[/i][/u][/size]

[b]Options Menu > Extension options > All Ships with Filters[/b]:
[list]
[*] [b]Debug mode[/b]: Controls log verbosity. Options: None (default), Debug, Trace. Use Debug or Trace only when troubleshooting - these write to the game log on every refresh.
[/list]
